{
    "pr_body": "Instead of using raw TCP sockets and parsing HTTP requests manually which is tends to be quite error-prone, we can create an HTTP proxy server using ApacheHttpServer. In contrast to `com.sun.net` an Apache HTTP server it can act as an HTTP proxy. \r\n\r\nThis change also allows the server to upport persistent keep-alive connections. It should prevent creating excessive threads to handle new HTTP connection which matters when we run heavy tests in `GcsProxyIntegrationTests.`\r\n\r\nIt's a more straighforward alternative to #93891.\r\n\r\nFixes https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/93824\r\nFixes https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/93811\r\nFixes https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/93816",
    "original_commit_id": "6e8744917d81fce7688851de02cdf77dbc4dbb8d",
    "merged": true,
    "pr_number": 94205,
    "pr_title": "Migrate MockHttpServer to Apache HttpServer",
